{
  "id": "05-product-of-array-except-self",
  "title": "Product of Array Except Self",
  "track": "Arrays",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "topics": [
    "arrays",
    "prefix-sums"
  ],
  "source": "canonical Product of Array Except Self concept; description, examples, and tests re-authored",
  "description": "The input is an array of integers nums. Return an array answer of the same length where answer[i] is the product of every element except nums[i]. Division is not allowed, so the answer must be built from multiplications only.",
  "constraints": [
    "2 <= len(nums) <= 1200",
    "-10 <= nums[i] <= 10",
    "for every position, the product of the other elements fits in a 64-bit signed integer"
  ],
  "parameters": [
    "nums"
  ],
  "functionName": "product_except_self",
  "starterCode": "def product_except_self(nums):\n    # Return [product of all except nums[i]] for each i, without dividing.\n    ...\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": {
        "nums": [
          2,
          3,
          4,
          5
        ]
      },
      "output": [
        60,
        40,
        30,
        24
      ],
      "explanation": "answer[0] = 3*4*5 = 60, answer[1] = 2*4*5 = 40, and so on."
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "nums": [
          2,
          0,
          4
        ]
      },
      "output": [
        0,
        8,
        0
      ],
      "explanation": "Every product that includes the zero collapses to 0; only position 1 skips it."
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "The product excluding position i splits into two parts: everything left of i, and everything right of i.",
    "Two sweeps can fill those parts: one pass accumulating products from the left, one from the right.",
    "Store left[i] = product of nums[0..i-1] and right[i] = product of nums[i+1..end]. The answer at i is left[i] * right[i]."
  ],
  "solution": "Build a prefix-product sweep and a suffix-product sweep. The value at each position is the product of all elements before it times the product of all elements after it, so no division is needed. Two passes plus the output: O(n) time, O(1) extra space beyond the result array.",
  "solutionCode": "def product_except_self(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    answer = [1] * n\n    left = 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        answer[i] = left\n        left *= nums[i]\n    right = 1\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        answer[i] *= right\n        right *= nums[i]\n    return answer\n",
  "bruteForceCode": "def product_except_self(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    answer = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        product = 1\n        for j in range(n):\n            if j != i:\n                product *= nums[j]\n        answer.append(product)\n    return answer\n",
  "failureHint": "hidden tests include zeros, negative values, and repeated values",
  "expectedComplexity": {
    "time": "O(n)",
    "space": "O(1)"
  },
